1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Welcome to the talk on writing maintainable code that your whole team can actually understand and safely change without fear of breaking something else.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,200
The first rule is to keep your functions small and focused, because a function that does one thing is far easier to test, debug, and reuse.

3
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,800
Name things clearly; a good name removes the need for a comment, and it helps the next reader build an accurate mental model quickly.
